    "created_at": "2021-10-12T14:59:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-10-12T14:59:22Z",
    "body": "Well, \"site for cookies\" itself is not conveyed to the server.  It simply takes part in determining if `SameSite=Strict` cookies, etc, are sent to the server.\r\n\r\nI do think, though, that if we had Sec-Fetch-Ancestors we could use that information for this as well.  (If its propagated through the fetch in a service worker.)  And of course since destination distinguishes between `document` and `iframe` it has the information as well, but it isn't propagated through the SW.",
